@Bookings.Api_HostAddress = http://localhost:5029

### CA1 - Create booking -> 201 + Location
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer":{
    "name":"miguel",
    "email":"mi@gu.el"
  },
  "start":"2026-12-01T10:00:00Z",
  "end":"2026-12-01T11:00:00Z",
  "resourceId":"room-A"
}

### F2 - List bookings with default sort and paging -> 200
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Accept: application/json

### CA9 - Filter by resource and overlapping range -> 200, only intersecting bookings
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?resourceId=room-A&from=2026-12-01T10:30:00Z&to=2026-12-01T12:00:00Z
Accept: application/json

### CA9 - Adjacent range [11:00, ...) does not intersect [10:00, 11:00) -> 200, empty
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?resourceId=room-A&from=2026-12-01T11:00:00Z
Accept: application/json

### F2 - Offset in query string, '+' encoded as %2B (11:30+01:00 = 10:30Z) -> 200
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?from=2026-12-01T11:30:00%2B01:00
Accept: application/json

### F2 - Sort by creation date descending, second page of one item -> 200
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?sort=-createdAt&page=2&pageSize=1
Accept: application/json

### F2 - Page size above max -> 400 errors.PageSize
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?pageSize=500
Accept: application/json

### F2 - Invalid sort -> 400 errors.Sort
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?sort=foo
Accept: application/json

### F2 - From after To -> 400 errors.To
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?from=2026-12-02T00:00:00Z&to=2026-12-01T00:00:00Z
Accept: application/json

### F2 - Unparseable page -> 400 code bad_request
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings?page=abc
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F3 - Confirm. Run the requests below in order, top to bottom.
# Booking A uses a random resource so the scenario can be re-run on a non-empty
# database; B and C reuse A's resource through request variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### CA2 - Create booking A (10:00-11:00) in a fresh resource -> 201
# @name createA
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Ana", "email": "ana@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-01-15T10:00:00Z",
  "end": "2027-01-15T11:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "room-{{$randomInt 100000 999999}}"
}

### CA2 - Confirm booking A, no overlap -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### CA3 - Create booking B (10:30-11:30) overlapping A in the same resource -> 201
# @name createB
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Bruno", "email": "bruno@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-01-15T10:30:00Z",
  "end": "2027-01-15T11:30:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{createA.request.body.$.resourceId}}"
}

### CA3 - Confirm B while A is confirmed -> 409 booking.overlap
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createB.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### CA4 - Create booking C (11:00-12:00) adjacent to A in the same resource -> 201
# @name createC
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Carla", "email": "carla@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-01-15T11:00:00Z",
  "end": "2027-01-15T12:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{createA.request.body.$.resourceId}}"
}

### CA4 - Confirm C, adjacent to A and overlapping only the pending B -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createC.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### F3 - Confirm A again, already confirmed -> 422 booking.invalid_transition
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createA.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### F3 - Confirm a booking that does not exist -> 404 booking.not_found
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/confirm
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F4 - Cancel. Run the requests below in order, top to bottom.
# Uses its own random resource, independent from the F3 scenario.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### F4 - Create booking D (09:00-10:00) in a fresh resource -> 201
# @name createD
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Diego", "email": "diego@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-02-10T09:00:00Z",
  "end": "2027-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "room-{{$randomInt 100000 999999}}"
}

### F4 - Cancel pending booking D with a reason -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createD.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "reason": "Customer called to cancel"
}

### CA5 - Cancel booking D again, already cancelled -> 422 booking.invalid_transition
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createD.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Accept: application/json

### F4 - Create booking E (09:00-10:00) in the same resource -> 201
# @name createE
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Elena", "email": "elena@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-02-10T09:00:00Z",
  "end": "2027-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{createD.request.body.$.resourceId}}"
}

### F4 - Confirm booking E -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createE.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### F4 - Cancel confirmed booking E without body (reason is optional) -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createE.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Accept: application/json

### F4 - Create booking F in the slot freed by E -> 201
# @name createF
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Fran", "email": "fran@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-02-10T09:00:00Z",
  "end": "2027-02-10T10:00:00Z",
  "resourceId": "{{createD.request.body.$.resourceId}}"
}

### F4 - Confirm F, cancelling E released the slot -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createF.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### F4 - Cancel with a reason longer than 100 characters -> 400 errors.Reason
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createF.response.body.$.id}}/cancel
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "reason": "This reason is intentionally far too long for the limit, so it must be rejected before reaching the domain."
}

### F4 - Cancel a booking that does not exist -> 404 booking.not_found
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001/cancel
Accept: application/json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# F5 - Booking details. Run the requests below in order, top to bottom.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

### F5 - Create booking G with a +02:00 offset -> 201 + Location
# @name createG
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "customer": { "name": "Gloria", "email": "gloria@example.com" },
  "start": "2027-04-01T09:00:00+02:00",
  "end": "2027-04-01T10:00:00+02:00",
  "resourceId": "room-{{$randomInt 100000 999999}}"
}

### F5 - Follow the Location header of the 201 -> 200, start persisted in UTC (07:00Z)
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}{{createG.response.headers.Location}}
Accept: application/json

### F5 - Confirm booking G -> 200
POST {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createG.response.body.$.id}}/confirm
Accept: application/json

### F5 - Get booking G after confirming -> 200, status Confirmed and confirmedAt set
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/{{createG.response.body.$.id}}
Accept: application/json

### F5 - Get a booking that does not exist -> 404 booking.not_found
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
Accept: application/json

### F5 - Get with an id that is not a GUID -> 404, the :guid route constraint does not match
GET {{Bookings.Api_HostAddress}}/api/bookings/abc
Accept: application/json
